# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# SatQuery AI — .gitignore
# Rules marked [LICENCE] exist to keep restricted imagery and
# mislicensed artifacts out of a public government deliverable.
# Read docs/README.md and CREDITS.md before relaxing any of them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST

# --- Virtual environments ---
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version

# --- Test / tooling caches ---
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/
.hypothesis/

# --- Notebooks ---
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb_checkpoints

# --- Editors / OS ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS — never commit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets.*
credentials.*
!satquery/credentials.py
kaggle.json
.kaggle/
.netrc
wandb/
.wandb/
*token*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# DATA — [LICENCE] staged imagery never enters the repo
# The manifest-first rule (master plan §2.2) means imagery is
# downloaded from its source, not redistributed by us.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Anchored to the repo root so training/data/ (source code) is NOT caught.
/data/
/datasets/
/staging/
*.tif
*.tiff
*.jp2
*.SAFE/
*.nc
*.hdf
*.h5
*.lmdb
*.mdb

# [LICENCE] HRSCD 2006 imagery is NON-REDISTRIBUTABLE (C60).
# It must come from IGN directly and must never appear in a repo,
# a demo, or a shipped artifact.
**/HRSCD/**
**/hrscd/**
**/*2006*.tif

# [LICENCE] VRSBench / DOTA-derived imagery is academic-only and
# must never enter training, the repo, or the public demo (C20).
**/VRSBench/**
**/vrsbench/**

# [LICENCE] Dropped sources — purged from all manifests (C56).
# Present here so a stray download cannot be committed by accident.
**/LEVIR*/**
**/SECOND/**
**/QAG-360K/**

# Generated timing fixtures. The 21 PNGs are CONSTANT BLACK dummies
# for shape-only timing — never training data. Regenerate with
# training/data/extract_ben_micro.py.
# NOTE: dataset-metadata.json in here declares CC0-1.0, which is
# WRONG for CDLA-Permissive-derived annotations. Fix before any
# upload. See TEAM_CONTEXT.md mistake #6.
ben-micro-split/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL ARTIFACTS
# Checkpoints go to the private HF repo (guard rail 2), not here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
*.pt
*.pth
*.bin
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.gguf
checkpoints/
outputs/
runs/
lightning_logs/
adapters/
hf_cache/
.cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# LOGS
# logs/*.md are curated measurement reports — those are TRACKED.
# Raw run output is not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
!logs/phase_0_timing_report.log
logs/**/*.jsonl
logs/tmp/

# Large per-item eval dumps and corpus review artifacts. Regenerable, and
# 21 MB of the 23 MB in logs/ sits in these five files alone. The curated
# measurement reports every number in docs/ cites are small JSON and stay
# tracked -- these are the raw intermediates behind them.
logs/_*.json
logs/corpus_review.html
logs/corpus_sample.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# HOUSEKEEPING
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
_to_delete/
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.7z
tmp/
scratch/

# Locally staged sample imagery. Referenced by
# `satquery/qgen/loaders/rareplanes.py` and the demo scripts, fetched
# with `sample_dataset/fetch_real.py` -- never redistributed by us.
sample_dataset_real/
/rareplanes_images/

# Tool output, regenerable: `/graphify` rebuilds it from the tree.
graphify-out/

# Superseded frontend, archived outside the repo. Kept as a rule so a
# stray copy cannot be committed.
frontend_pre_merge/

# Agent/editor workspace. `launch.json` is useful project config and is
# whitelisted; session state is not.
.claude/*
!.claude/launch.json

# The testing-corpus gallery: 275 images + previews, published to the
# Modal Volume rather than the repo. Regenerate with
# `scripts/build_gallery.py select && ... fetch`.
/data/gallery/

# --- Frontend (when the app lands) ---
node_modules/
.next/
.nuxt/
.svelte-kit/
.turbo/
*.local
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# --- Internal working documents ---
# Kept locally, not shipped. The planning tree, the per-capability
# engineering record, the paper material and the deck are working
# documents; TEAM_CONTEXT.md is onboarding notes including the mistake
# log. None of it is part of the product.
# `/docs/*`, not `/docs/`: git does not descend into an excluded directory, so
# a negation inside one can never take effect. Excluding the contents instead
# leaves the directory readable and lets the one file below be re-included.
/docs/*
# The benchmark comparison is the one document a reviewer asks for, and the
# README links to it. The rest of docs/ stays local.
!/docs/BENCHMARKS.md
TEAM_CONTEXT.md
